                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>What is a healthy Amazon ACoS?</h3>
                                        <p>15-30% typical for profitable Amazon Ads. Depends on category + margin + stage. Growth stage may accept 30-40%. Below 15% could indicate under-investment.</p>
                                        <h3>ACoS vs TACoS — which matters more?</h3>
                                        <p>Both. ACoS for campaign-level efficiency + TACoS for total-business advertising efficiency + advertising-organic relationship.</p>
                                        <h3>Should D2C brands be Amazon-only?</h3>
                                        <p>Rarely optimal. Amazon + brand.com + Meta + Google combined typical. Amazon for discovery + volume + brand.com for retention + LTV.</p>
                                        <h3>What is the biggest Amazon Ads mistake?</h3>
                                        <p>Ignoring TACoS + poor keyword targeting + no brand defense. All three destroy budget efficiency + business economics.</p>
